@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0141>
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:notation "dpp-0141" ;
  skos:prefLabel "trigger predicate"@eng ;
  skos:definition "declared component of a profile stating the conditions under which the profile applies, evaluated against the facts of the digital twin rather than against who declares them"@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Characteristic profiles (concept dpp-0125) attach by predicate on twin facts — age, material content, heritage status, market status — rather than by law-of-place or industry."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Predicate triggers include time predicates: an object becoming older than a given age is a clock-fired applicability event, handled by the dated-binding machinery so that applicability attaches without human declaration."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "The expression \"characteristic profile trigger\" denotes this predicate as used by a characteristic profile and is folded into this concept rather than recorded separately."@eng
 .